.TH geectl-branch-create 1  "geectl-branch-create 0.2.4" 
.SH NAME
geectl\-branch\-create \- Branch a git\-backed package: Gitea fork + OBS fork into a test project with the source project\*(Aqs repositories. A mutation: dry\-run is the default (only the plan is printed); `\-\-live` performs the branch
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgeectl branch create\fR [\fB\-\-new\-repo\-name\fR] [\fB\-\-organization\fR] [\fB\-\-git\-branch\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-devel\-project\fR] [\fB\-\-target\-project\fR] [\fB\-\-target\-package\fR] [\fB\-\-first\-build\-deadline\-secs\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fB\-\-project\fR> <\fB\-\-package\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Branch a git\-backed package: Gitea fork + OBS fork into a test project with the source project\*(Aqs repositories. A mutation: dry\-run is the default (only the plan is printed); `\-\-live` performs the branch
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-project\fR \fI<PROJECT>\fR
The project to branch from
.TP
\fB\-\-package\fR \fI<PACKAGE>\fR
The package to branch
.TP
\fB\-\-new\-repo\-name\fR \fI<NEW_REPO_NAME>\fR
Name for the fork; defaults to the source repo name
.TP
\fB\-\-organization\fR \fI<ORGANIZATION>\fR
Organization to fork into; defaults to the token owner\*(Aqs account
.TP
\fB\-\-git\-branch\fR \fI<GIT_BRANCH>\fR
Branch to fork from and name in the fork\*(Aqs scmsync URL; defaults to the source branch
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-devel\-project\fR
Ignore the devel project when resolving the fork source
.TP
\fB\-\-target\-project\fR \fI<TARGET_PROJECT>\fR
The branch project. Without it, the server picks the default (usually `home:<user>:branches:<source project>`)
.TP
\fB\-\-target\-package\fR \fI<TARGET_PACKAGE>\fR
The branch package name. Without it, the source package name
.TP
\fB\-\-first\-build\-deadline\-secs\fR \fI<FIRST_BUILD_DEADLINE_SECS>\fR [default: 0]
Seconds to wait for the first build of the forked package in the fork\*(Aqs test project; 0 skips the wait and reports the branch without a build. No wait by default
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH VERSION
v0.2.4
